  message: "FOLD 2026-09-30 (owner delegated the decision): WI-hijot-sosak (P4 someday, \"INV-dihos Phase 3 (split): Return-Type Registry for Scala\", filed 05-26) is folded INTO this item. It prescribes exactly this item's call-result + chained-receiver half; this item is the superset (adds for-binder and lambda parameter), is P2, and carries the measured baseline and the current premise check.\nWhat WI-hijot contributes, now part of this item's scope:\n- Deliverables: populate FileAnalysis.method_return_types from each function_definition's signature in Pass 1; consult the BASE registry (self._method_return_type_registry, base.py ~4446-4458) in the Pass-2 var_types fill loop; add a typed-variable method-call strategy in _extract_edges_scala mirroring Rust's.\n- A `_extract_scala_return_type_name` helper with: `def f(...): T` extraction; generic strip (`List[T]`/`Map[K,V]` -> `List`/`Map`; scala uses [T]); unwrap of Option[T] / Try[T] / Future[T] / Either[L,R] (right-biased), analogous to Rust Option/Result; implicits explicitly deferred.\n- Its cited `scala.py:613-647` (var_types bootstrap) is stale; the current binders are at scala.py ~1363-1392 per the premise check above.\n- DEPENDENCY CARRIED OVER: WI-hijot was `isbefore` WI-hudam (INV-dihos Phase 4, Python registry). That edge reads as campaign phase ordering rather than a hard dependency, but it is transferred here unchanged rather than dropped; WI-hudam is also still blocked by WI-zimat.\nStill separate (related, not folded): WI-jubim (P3), the library-row half."  # c70e
