  message: "WORK DONE 2026-10-01 (concurrent run; NOT integrated, no PR). Branch jgstern-agent/feat/gokop-scala-inferred-receivers in ~/hg_wt/gokop, commits b276267a67 (feat) + 5d15bfd294 (fix). Status left unchanged.\n\nWHAT: scala.py Pass 1 now fills the base return-type registry (declared def return types; typed member vals and class params as parameterless members; qualified through the DECLARING file's imports; implicit-import names and type params refused; this.type -> owner; Future[T]/Try[T] register as the wrapper, never T) plus a scala-local ELEMENT registry (Seq[File] -> File; Either right-biased). Pass 2 types receivers through a new _ScalaReceiverTyper: nearest lexical binder first (lambda, case, for, param, class param, block/template val), falling back to the old file-wide map when that binder's type cannot be said; call results, chains, parameterless members a.b, this, asInstanceOf[T], case-class apply; elements type for-generators, one-param lambdas / whole-pattern case / placeholder _ of element-passing calls, and .get/.head/.getOrElse projections. A qualified project type binds only where the WI-tipoh _import_names_elsewhere check allows. ADR-0006 Scala row filled in.\n\nMEASURED (A/B in one process, origin/dev scala.py vs HEAD scala.py, same core; instrument = pokam's metric over unresolved scala calls edges with call_construct=method):\n  sbt : hinted 19.74% (3,893/19,723) -> 24.61% (4,682/19,023); slot 21.31% -> 23.76%; resolved calls 10,095 -> 10,795 (+700); calls_total 39,343 both.\n  lila: hinted  7.62% (3,363/44,137) -> 12.18% (5,145/42,245); slot 5.99% -> 6.47%; resolved 15,246 -> 17,138 (+1,892); calls_total 84,675 both.\n  Per call site: hints lost 0 / 0; newly UNresolved 0 / 0; newly resolved bound to an implicitly-imported owner 0 / 0 (it was 2 on sbt -- Map(pairs*) -> project SessionVar.Map.get -- before the guard). Newly resolved whose owner's simple name is declared in >1 file: sbt 84, lila 702; a 30-edge sample of those read against source found none wrong (not a precision measurement of the rest).\n  Baseline moved since filing: sbt 9.03%->19.74% and lila 4.50%->7.62% hinted on origin/dev today (denominator 15,872->19,723 / 38,008->44,137).\nWHAT IT DOES NOT ESTABLISH: precision of newly HINTED (unresolved) types beyond the samples; for-binder/lambda typing barely moved on the corpus (lila for_binder un-hinted 475 -> 465, lambda_param 296 -> 276) because element types need a declared container type and lila writes Fu[A] aliases and undeclared defs.\nRESIDUALS FILED: WI-kipol (P2, bare project-object calls, the largest remaining bucket: sbt 2,564 / lila 2,779 un-hinted), WI-modib (P3, defs with no declared return type: lila 52%, sbt 14%), WI-koraz (P3, type aliases: 1,016 lila hints are Fu/Funit). Notes on WI-niriz (refused cross-package binds it would recover) and WI-jubim (scala now reads library_signatures; a scala.yaml is what remains).\nTESTS: targeted smart-test 9503 passed, 1 xfailed, scala.py 100% covered (303 affected test files). New tests/test_scala_return_type_registry.py; test_scala_receiver_type_module_slot.py's nameless-receiver pin updated (new File(p) now slots java.io.File; fetch() stays the sentinel control)."  # d0c1
